  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Your friend works as a valet where NNN cars show up in a shift. The iii-th car will arrive TiT_iTi​ seconds after the current moment, and the car can wait for at most YiY_iYi​ seconds. That is, your friend can only start parking the car from time TiT_iTi​ to Ti+YiT_i+Y_iTi​+Yi​ (inclusive).\n\nAdditionally, it takes XiX_iXi​ time to park the iii-th car, which means he cannot park any other cars for XiX_iXi​ seconds starting from the time he starts parking the iii-th car. It is known that no driver would like to wait for more time than it takes to park his car, so that Yi&lt;XiY_i  &lt; X_iYi​&lt;Xi​ for all iii. The driver of the iii-th car will pay AiA_iAi​ coins as a tip to your friend if his car is parked. Note that he can start parking the next car immediately after he finishes parking the previous car.\n\nYour friend has asked you what will be the maximize possible earnings if he optimally chooses which cars to park and at what times.\n\n###Input:\n\n\n\nThe first line contains one single integer NNN (1≤N≤3⋅105)(1 \\le N \\le 3 \\cdot 10^5)(1≤N≤3⋅105) −-− the number of cars.\n\n\n\n\nThe second line contains NNN integers T1,T2,…,TnT_1, T_2, \\ldots, T_nT1​,T2​,…,Tn​ −-− the time (in seconds) at which iii-th car arrives.\n\n\n\n\nThe third line contains NNN integers X1,X2,…,XnX_1, X_2, \\ldots, X_nX1​,X2​,…,Xn​ −-− the time (in seconds) required to park the iii-th car.\n\n\n\n\nThe fourth line contains NNN integers Y1,Y2,…,YnY_1, Y_2, \\ldots, Y_nY1​,Y2​,…,Yn​ −-− the maximum time (in seconds) for which the iii-th car can wait.\n\n\n\n\nThe fifth line contains NNN integers A1,A2,…,AnA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_nA1​,A2​,…,An​ −-− the tip which the iii-th car driver gives after the car is parked.\n\n\n\n###Output:\r\nPrint a single integer −-− the answer to the problem.\n\n###Constraints\n\n\n\n1≤N≤3⋅1051\\le N\\le 3\\cdot 10^51≤N≤3⋅105\n\n\n\n\n1≤Ti≤4⋅1031\\le T_i\\le 4\\cdot 10^31≤Ti​≤4⋅103\n\n\n\n\n0≤Yi&lt;Xi≤4⋅1030\\le Y_i &lt; X_i\\le 4\\cdot 10^30≤Yi​&lt;Xi​≤4⋅103\n\n\n\n\n1≤Ai≤1091\\le A_i\\le 10^91≤Ai​≤109",
